CORE
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ pointer declarator: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ reference declarator: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
substitute_function_type and convert_function_template_declaration built
the parameters' placeholder symbols from pdecl.type(); they now merge the
declarator.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
